  "_readme": [
    "Reference manifest of Supabase Edge Functions currently deployed to the",
    "live project (jjyyfaxcwanrmiipzkoj), fetched via the Supabase Management",
    "API using a personal access token (not through this repo's own tooling).",
    "This is metadata only — slug, version, verify_jwt, timestamps, and (where",
    "present) a content sha256 — never function source code and never a",
    "secret/token. It exists for the same reason supabase/schema.sql does: so",
    "a session (sandbox or otherwise) can see what's actually live without",
    "asking the user to re-paste a fresh API dump every time.",
    "",
    "This file goes stale the moment a function is deployed, renamed, or",
    "removed outside of a session that remembers to refresh it. Treat",
    "'updated_at' per function, plus the 'fetched_at' below, as the only real",
    "freshness signal — if a task depends on a function's exact current",
    "behavior, re-fetch or read its live source rather than trusting this file",
    "blindly for anything beyond \"does a function with this slug exist / what",
    "was its last known version\".",
    "",
    "Local entrypoint_path values reflect the path on whichever machine last",
    "deployed that function (several read /Users/user/..., /Users/USER/...,",
    "or a /tmp/user_fn_... path for functions last deployed via the dashboard",
    "editor rather than the CLI) — these are informational only, not paths",
    "that exist in this repo or resolve on any other machine.",
    "",
    "Update process: re-fetch the function list via the Management API (or",
    "`supabase functions list` with the project linked), replace the",
    "'functions' array and 'fetched_at' below, and commit — same patch/git am",
    "handoff process as any other repo file (this is not a schema.sql-style",
    "direct-push exception; it doesn't come from pg_dump or require live DB",
    "credentials to produce)."
  ],
